px;height:24px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-home"><path d="M10 20v-6h4v6h5v-8h3L12 3 2 12h3v8z"></path></svg></a></span></li><li class="flex items-center text-grey-40 "><span class="flex px-1"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:16px;height:16px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_right"><path d="M10 6L8.59 7.41 13.17 12l-4.58 4.59L10 18l6-6-6-6z"></path></svg></span><a href="/first-aid" class="relative items-center w-fit normal-case text-sm antialiased decoration-1 text-grey-40 hover:underline focus:underline underline-offset-4 underline hover:decoration-3 hover:text-black-primary" data-analytics-id="breadcrumb_link">First aid</a></li><li class="flex items-center text-grey-40 "><span class="flex px-1"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:16px;height:16px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_right"><path d="M10 6L8.59 7.41 13.17 12l-4.58 4.59L10 18l6-6-6-6z"></path></svg></span><a href="/first-aid/learn-first-aid" class="relative items-center w-fit normal-case text-sm antialiased decoration-1 text-grey-40 hover:underline focus:underline underline-offset-4 underline hover:decoration-3 hover:text-black-primary" data-analytics-id="breadcrumb_link">Learn first aid</a></li><li class="flex items-center text-grey-40 "><span class="flex px-1"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:16px;height:16px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_right"><path d="M10 6L8.59 7.41 13.17 12l-4.58 4.59L10 18l6-6-6-6z"></path></svg></span><p class="text-sm text-grey-40 font-normal antialiased normal-case" aria-current="page">Strains and sprains</p></li></ol></nav></div><main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="px-4"><section lang="en" class="brc-standard-hero relative brc-hero brc-neg-mx-4 mb-8 px-4 md:mb-12 bg-white"><div class="max-content mx-auto grid items-center grid-cols-12 gap-4 lg:gap-6 py-6 md:py-8 border-grey-20 border-b"><div class="z-[1] col-span-12 prose-h1:mb-2 prose-h1:md:mb-4 md:col-span-9 lg:col-span-8"><h1 id="strain-or-a-sprain-first-aid">Strain or a sprain: first aid</h1><p class="text-base md:text-xl">Adult first aid for someone who has a strain or sprain including signs and what to do in an emergency.</p></div></div></section><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><h2 id="what-is-a-strain-or-sprain">What is a strain or sprain?</h2><p>If someone has pain, swelling or bruising around a joint or muscle after a sudden movement to part of their body, they may have a sprain or strain.</p><h2 id="signs-and-symptoms-of-a-sprain-or-strain">Signs and symptoms of a sprain or strain</h2><p>Strains and sprains happen when someone suddenly moves part of their body. Around a joint or muscle they may have:</p><ul><li>pain</li><li>swelling</li><li>bruising</li><li>if the injury is at a joint, the person may have difficulty in moving a limb</li></ul></div></div><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><h2 id="first-aid-steps-for-someone-with-a-strain-or-sprain">First aid steps for someone with a strain or sprain</h2><h3 id="1-get-the-person-to-rest">1. Get the person to rest.</h3></div></div><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><h3 id="2-apply-an-ice-pack-to-the-injury">2. Apply an ice pack to the injury.</h3><p>An ice pack could be ice or frozen vegetables wrapped in a tea towel. Applying it to the injury will reduce the swelling and pain.</p></div></div><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><h3 id="3-if-there-is-no-improvement-seek-medical-advice">3. If there is no improvement, seek medical advice.</h3></div></div><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><h3 id="watch-how-to-help-someone-who-has-a-sprain-or-strain-1-minute-56-seconds">Watch how to help someone who has a sprain or strain (1 minute 56 seconds)</h3></div></div><div class="brc-video brc-layout-container mb-8 md:mb-12 lg:mb-16" lang="en"><figure><div><noscript><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3CEiFmVzzyc" aria-label="Watch Play Video on YouTube">Watch &quot;<!-- -->Play Video<!-- -->&quot; on YouTube</a></noscript><article class="yt-lite " data-title="Play Video" role="img" aria-label="Play Video - YouTube video preview" style="background-image:url(https://i.ytimg.com/vi/3CEiFmVzzyc/hqdefault.jpg);--aspect-ratio:56.25%"><button type="button" class="lty-playbtn" aria-label="Watch Play Video" tabindex="0"><span class="lty-visually-hidden">Watch</span></button></article></div></figure></div><div class="max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12 lg:mb-16" lang="en"><div class="max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8"><div class="mb-4 md:mb-6"><h2 id="common-questions-about-first-aid-someone-who-has-a-strain-or-sprain">Common questions about first aid someone who has a strain or sprain</h2></div><section class="border-2 border-b-1 border-solid border-grey-40 focus:border-green-primary active:hover:border-green-primary focus-within:border-green-primary"><div class="border-b border-grey-40"><details lang="en"><summary class="group list-none w-full pointer-events-auto py-4 px-6 text-left text-sm hover:text-white hover:bg-blue-secondary focus:text-white focus:bg-blue-secondary focus:outline-none md:text-base brc-no-summary-triangle"><div class="flex w-full items-start justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border-2 border-transparent group-focus:border-green-primary group-hover:text-white"><h3 id="whats-the-difference-between-a-strain-and-a-sprain" class="text-sm font-normal m-0 group-hover:text-white group-focus:text-white md:text-base">What’s the difference between a strain and a sprain?</h3><span class="ml-6 flex h-7 items-center text-sm md:text-base rtl:ml-0 rtl:mr-6"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:24px;height:24px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_down"><path d="M12 15.586L6.707 10.293L5.293 11.707L12 18.414L18.707 11.707L17.293 10.293L12 15.586Z"></path></svg></span></div></summary><div class="py-4 px-7 border-t border-grey-40 brc-accordion-section-text"><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>A strain is when a muscle is damaged. A sprain is when a joint – such as a knee, ankle or wrist – is damaged.</p></div></div></div></details></div><div class="border-b border-grey-40"><details lang="en"><summary class="group list-none w-full pointer-events-auto py-4 px-6 text-left text-sm hover:text-white hover:bg-blue-secondary focus:text-white focus:bg-blue-secondary focus:outline-none md:text-base brc-no-summary-triangle"><div class="flex w-full items-start justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border-2 border-transparent group-focus:border-green-primary group-hover:text-white"><h3 id="is-there-anything-other-than-ice-that-i-can-use-to-help-with-a-sprain-or-strain" class="text-sm font-normal m-0 group-hover:text-white group-focus:text-white md:text-base">Is there anything other than ice that I can use to help with a sprain or strain?</h3><span class="ml-6 flex h-7 items-center text-sm md:text-base rtl:ml-0 rtl:mr-6"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:24px;height:24px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_down"><path d="M12 15.586L6.707 10.293L5.293 11.707L12 18.414L18.707 11.707L17.293 10.293L12 15.586Z"></path></svg></span></div></summary><div class="py-4 px-7 border-t border-grey-40 brc-accordion-section-text"><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>You can use something cold, such as frozen vegetables wrapped in a tea towel.</p></div></div></div></details></div><div class="border-b border-grey-40"><details lang="en"><summary class="group list-none w-full pointer-events-auto py-4 px-6 text-left text-sm hover:text-white hover:bg-blue-secondary focus:text-white focus:bg-blue-secondary focus:outline-none md:text-base brc-no-summary-triangle"><div class="flex w-full items-start justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border-2 border-transparent group-focus:border-green-primary group-hover:text-white"><h3 id="how-long-should-i-apply-an-ice-pack-to-the-injury-for" class="text-sm font-normal m-0 group-hover:text-white group-focus:text-white md:text-base">How long should I apply an ice pack to the injury for?</h3><span class="ml-6 flex h-7 items-center text-sm md:text-base rtl:ml-0 rtl:mr-6"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:24px;height:24px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_down"><path d="M12 15.586L6.707 10.293L5.293 11.707L12 18.414L18.707 11.707L17.293 10.293L12 15.586Z"></path></svg></span></div></summary><div class="py-4 px-7 border-t border-grey-40 brc-accordion-section-text"><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>Apply the ice pack to the injury for no more than 10 minutes. Anything over 10 minutes can cause further damage.</p></div></div></div></details></div><div class="border-b border-grey-40"><details lang="en"><summary class="group list-none w-full pointer-events-auto py-4 px-6 text-left text-sm hover:text-white hover:bg-blue-secondary focus:text-white focus:bg-blue-secondary focus:outline-none md:text-base brc-no-summary-triangle"><div class="flex w-full items-start justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border-2 border-transparent group-focus:border-green-primary group-hover:text-white"><h3 id="what-do-i-do-after-i-have-put-an-ice-pack-on-the-injury" class="text-sm font-normal m-0 group-hover:text-white group-focus:text-white md:text-base">What do I do after I have put an ice pack on the injury?</h3><span class="ml-6 flex h-7 items-center text-sm md:text-base rtl:ml-0 rtl:mr-6"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:24px;height:24px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_down"><path d="M12 15.586L6.707 10.293L5.293 11.707L12 18.414L18.707 11.707L17.293 10.293L12 15.586Z"></path></svg></span></div></summary><div class="py-4 px-7 border-t border-grey-40 brc-accordion-section-text"><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>Keep the injured part of the body supported in a raised position. Then apply a bandage around the injury. The bandage should not be tightly wrapped and you should make sure the bandage does not become tight.</p></div></div></div></details></div><div class="border-b border-grey-40"><details lang="en"><summary class="group list-none w-full pointer-events-auto py-4 px-6 text-left text-sm hover:text-white hover:bg-blue-secondary focus:text-white focus:bg-blue-secondary focus:outline-none md:text-base brc-no-summary-triangle"><div class="flex w-full items-start justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border-2 border-transparent group-focus:border-green-primary group-hover:text-white"><h3 id="is-the-acronym-rice-still-used-for-helping-someone-with-a-strain-or-sprain" class="text-sm font-normal m-0 group-hover:text-white group-focus:text-white md:text-base">Is the acronym RICE still used for helping someone with a strain or sprain?</h3><span class="ml-6 flex h-7 items-center text-sm md:text-base rtl:ml-0 rtl:mr-6"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:24px;height:24px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_down"><path d="M12 15.586L6.707 10.293L5.293 11.707L12 18.414L18.707 11.707L17.293 10.293L12 15.586Z"></path></svg></span></div></summary><div class="py-4 px-7 border-t border-grey-40 brc-accordion-section-text"><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>Yes, RICE is a great way to remember how to help someone with a strain or sprain. The letters in RICE stand for:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Rest</li>
  <li>Ice</li>
  <li>Comfortable support</li>
  <li>Elevate.</li>
</ul>
<p>Comfortable support can include an elasticated bandage around the affected joint or limb.</p></div></div></div></details></div><div class="border-b border-grey-40"><details lang="en"><summary class="group list-none w-full pointer-events-auto py-4 px-6 text-left text-sm hover:text-white hover:bg-blue-secondary focus:text-white focus:bg-blue-secondary focus:outline-none md:text-base brc-no-summary-triangle"><div class="flex w-full items-start justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border-2 border-transparent group-focus:border-green-primary group-hover:text-white"><h3 id="can-you-use-a-warm-cloth-or-alternate-between-warm-and-cold-treatment" class="text-sm font-normal m-0 group-hover:text-white group-focus:text-white md:text-base">Can you use a warm cloth or alternate between warm and cold treatment?</h3><span class="ml-6 flex h-7 items-center text-sm md:text-base rtl:ml-0 rtl:mr-6"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:24px;height:24px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_down"><path d="M12 15.586L6.707 10.293L5.293 11.707L12 18.414L18.707 11.707L17.293 10.293L12 15.586Z"></path></svg></span></div></summary><div class="py-4 px-7 border-t border-grey-40 brc-accordion-section-text"><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>Warm treatments are not recommended first aid. An ice pack is the most effective way of reducing the swelling.</p></div></div></div></details></div><div class="border-b border-grey-40"><details lang="en"><summary class="group list-none w-full pointer-events-auto py-4 px-6 text-left text-sm hover:text-white hover:bg-blue-secondary focus:text-white focus:bg-blue-secondary focus:outline-none md:text-base brc-no-summary-triangle"><div class="flex w-full items-start justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border-2 border-transparent group-focus:border-green-primary group-hover:text-white"><h3 id="should-i-call-999-for-a-strain-or-sprain" class="text-sm font-normal m-0 group-hover:text-white group-focus:text-white md:text-base">Should I call 999 for a strain or sprain?</h3><span class="ml-6 flex h-7 items-center text-sm md:text-base rtl:ml-0 rtl:mr-6"><svg aria-hidden="true" style="width:24px;height:24px;fill:#717171" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="bg-blue-secondary" data-testid="svg-icon-chevron_down"><path d="M12 15.586L6.707 10.293L5.293 11.707L12 18.414L18.707 11.707L17.293 10.293L12 15.586Z"></path></svg></span></div></summary><div class="py-4 px-7 border-t border-grey-40 brc-accordion-section-text"><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>Most strains and sprains will feel better after rest and cooling.</p>
<p>Seek medical advice <a href="https://www.redcross.org.uk/first-aid/learn-first-aid/broken-bone" data-analytics-id="link">if you suspect that the bone is broken</a>, there are other injuries, or the injury does not improve.</p></div></div></div></details></div></section></div></div><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>For more information on how to help someone (or yourself) with a strain or sprain, visit the <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/sprains-and-strains/" data-analytics-id="link">NHS website.</a> During life-threatening emergencies, call 999, or for non-emergency medical help, call 111.</p><p>Have our First Aid app? Open it to try the quiz and test your knowledge. If you don&#x27;t have it, <a href="https://www.redcross.org.uk/first-aid/first-aid-apps" data-analytics-id="link">download the app and start learning</a>.</p><h2 id="more-first-aid-skills">More first aid skills:</h2><p><a href="https://www.redcross.org.uk/first-aid/learn-first-aid/bleeding-heavily" data-analytics-id="link">Bleeding heavily first aid</a></p><p><a href="https://www.redcross.org.uk/first-aid/learn-first-aid/asthma-attack" data-analytics-id="link">Asthma attack first aid</a></p></div></div><section class="brc-layout-container pb-8 md:pb-16" lang="en"><div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6 text-center"><div class="col-start-1 col-span-12 lg:col-start-3 pb-6 lg:col-span-8 md:pb-12"><h2 id="you-might-also-want-to">You might also want to:</h2><p class="text-sm md:text-base"></p></div></div><ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 auto-rows-fr md:grid-cols-2"><li lang="en" class="border border-grey-20  list-none flex flex-col group relative shadow-lg transition ease-in-out delay-150 duration-300 hover:scale-105 hover:shadow-xl focus:shadow-xl rtl:text-right "><div class="w-full prose-img:w-full prose-img:aspect-[4/3] prose-img:object-cover"><img src="https://assets.redcross.org.uk/82b1e254-5524-0172-0612-9ce813c7824c/f464e93c-b7b5-4864-8a82-7daadf28cc44/First-aid-app.png?w=528&amp;h=396&amp;fit=clip&amp;rect=136,0,812,610&amp;auto=format" alt="Close-up shot of a man&#x27;s hand holding an iPhone with the British Red Cross First Aid App open on the screen." class="w-full h-auto" loading="auto" fetchPriority="auto" srcSet="https://assets.redcross.org.uk/82b1e254-5524-0172-0612-9ce813c7824c/f464e93c-b7b5-4864-8a82-7daadf28cc44/First-aid-app.png?w=735&amp;h=551&amp;fit=clip&amp;rect=136,0,812,610&amp;auto=format 735w, https://assets.redcross.org.uk/82b1e254-5524-0172-0612-9ce813c7824c/f464e93c-b7b5-4864-8a82-7daadf28cc44/First-aid-app.png?w=484&amp;h=363&amp;fit=clip&amp;rect=136,0,812,610&amp;auto=format 484w, https://assets.redcross.org.uk/82b1e254-5524-0172-0612-9ce813c7824c/f464e93c-b7b5-4864-8a82-7daadf28cc44/First-aid-app.png?w=528&amp;h=396&amp;fit=clip&amp;rect=136,0,812,610&amp;auto=format 528w" sizes="(max-width: 767px) 735px, (max-width: 1023px) 484px, 528px"/></div><div class="w-full h-full flex flex-col justify-between px-6 pt-6 pb-8"><div><h3 class="mb-0"><a class="no-underline" href="/first-aid/first-aid-apps" data-analytics-id="card"><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0"></span>Try the First aid apps</a></h3><div class="prose-p:line-clamp-4 mt-4"><p class="text-sm md:text-base">Simple first aid skills are only two taps away. Our British Red Cross first aid apps allows you quickly access up-to-date information of help someone in a first aid emergency. Available for adults, and children and babies.</p></div></div><div></div></div></li><li lang="en" class="border border-grey-20  list-none flex flex-col group relative shadow-lg transition ease-in-out delay-150 duration-300 hover:scale-105 hover:shadow-xl focus:shadow-xl rtl:text-right "><div class="w-full prose-img:w-full prose-img:aspect-[4/3] prose-img:object-cover"><img src="https://assets.redcross.org.uk/82b1e254-5524-0172-0612-9ce813c7824c/87d9e73c-0c51-4c51-b06c-93cdf7da4c5f/RS22650-man-checking-breathing-first-aid-demonstration.jpg?w=528&amp;h=396&amp;fit=clip&amp;rect=66,0,1068,800&amp;auto=format" alt="A person kneels beside a man lying on the ground, checking his breathing during a first aid demonstration." class="w-full h-auto" loading="auto" fetchPriority="auto" srcSet="https://assets.redcross.org.uk/82b1e254-5524-0172-0612-9ce813c7824c/87d9e73c-0c51-4c51-b06c-93cdf7da4c5f/RS22650-man-checking-breathing-first-aid-demonstration.jpg?w=735&amp;h=551&amp;fit=clip&amp;rect=66,0,1068,800&amp;auto=format 735w, https://assets.redcross.org.uk/82b1e254-5524-0172-0612-9ce813c7824c/87d9e73c-0c51-4c51-b06c-93cdf7da4c5f/RS22650-man-checking-breathing-first-aid-demonstration.jpg?w=484&amp;h=363&amp;fit=clip&amp;rect=66,0,1068,800&amp;auto=format 484w, https://assets.redcross.org.uk/82b1e254-5524-0172-0612-9ce813c7824c/87d9e73c-0c51-4c51-b06c-93cdf7da4c5f/RS22650-man-checking-breathing-first-aid-demonstration.jpg?w=528&amp;h=396&amp;fit=clip&amp;rect=66,0,1068,800&amp;auto=format 528w" sizes="(max-width: 767px) 735px, (max-width: 1023px) 484px, 528px"/></div><div class="w-full h-full flex flex-col justify-between px-6 pt-6 pb-8"><div><h3 class="mb-0"><a class="no-underline" href="https://www.redcross.org.uk/first-aid/book-a-first-aid-course" data-analytics-id="card"><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0"></span>Book an accredited first aid course</a></h3><div class="prose-p:line-clamp-4 mt-4"><p class="text-sm md:text-base">Explore our range of paid training courses for the workplace.</p></div></div><div></div></div></li></ul></section></main><!--$--><!--/$--><div data-testid="pre-footer" class="border-t border-grey-30 px-4 pt-6 md:pt-8"><div class="brc-richtext-container max-content mx-auto grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-12"><div class="brc-richtext max-w-full col-span-12 col-start-1 md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-0"><p>Do you have a question about this page or want to giv